msgid "Debugging with GDB on STM32"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:7
#: 7af79ab8c2c04b28bf289f3d215c49e9
msgid "This page describes how to setup GDB on Linux to debug issues on STM32. The specific commands were tested on Ubuntu 18.10."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:10
#: 2849dbb50b0d41139a205f145b497087
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:12
#: fda8bf16899a4aa2bb1bf29d8d346b3a
msgid "GDB (the GNU Debugger) allows you to see what is going on inside another program while it executes or what another program was doing at the moment it crashed which can be useful when investigating very low-level failures with the STM32"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:17
#: 4c0f5c26b1d54683a8bfecc3e7af5c32
msgid "This guide assumes that you have already successfully built the firmware on your machine following the instructions for :ref:`Windows <building-setup-windows>`, :ref:`Mac <building-setup-mac>` or :ref:`Linux <building-setup-linux>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:20
#: a772fdffd475494897485ea6d6a6c887
msgid "One the the following debuggers is required:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:22
#: 08bf68c383274639aed569dc27ded829
msgid "`BlackMagic probe <http://www.blacksphere.co.nz/main/index.php/blackmagic>`__ (available from `1 Bit Squared <http://1bitsquared.com/collections/frontpage/products/black-magic-probe>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:23
#: 1fdc2be9dc1d499da070982ce6533932
msgid "`ST-Link V2 JST debugger <https://www.ebay.com/sch/i.html?_nkw=ST-Link-V2-Stlink-Emulator-Downloader-Programming-Mini-Unit-STM8-STM32>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:24
#: efb43c418edb457b8d080cd0e6eb83a3
msgid "`VM Probe <https://dev.vimdrones.com/products/vimdrones_stlinkv3_probe/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:26
#: 404dde524e0b42fcaf6391c87df4e0d0
msgid "A small plug (`FTSH-105-04-L-DV <https://au.element14.com/samtec/ftsh-105-04-l-dv/connector-header-1-27mm-smt-10way/dp/2308438?scope=partnumberlookahead&ost=FTSH-105-04-L-DV&searchref=searchlookahead&exaMfpn=true&ddkey=https%3Aen-AU%2FElement14_Australia%2Fw%2Fsearch>`__) may be required to solder on to the JTAG port of the flight controller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:30
#: 44b923e745c64964b464f9df4ace90f2
msgid "Compiling the Firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:32
#: b47d51051b554976b26211b5a0a27ec1
msgid "Build and upload the debug variant of the firmware:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:34
#: 1bb30bdf831a4f4cb02f8f342683ddc1
msgid "``` ./waf configure --board=Pixhawk1-1M --debug --enable-asserts ./waf --target=examples/UART_test --upload ```"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:40
#: a7569732e8de4ed5a0d1aef40083b7ae
msgid "Connecting the BlackMagic probe to the Pixhawk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:45
#: d8df2a9c122b4117a5d716aa1d489d44
msgid "The BlackMagic probe should be connected to the Pixhawk's JTAG connector using the grey 10wire cable that came with the probe. Note that most Pixhawk come with no headers soldered onto the JTAG connector because it interferes with the case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:51
#: 01188039fa92490f935716cad952b91c
msgid "Connecting the ST-Link V2 JTAG debugger to the STM32"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:56
#: dfa98a82604447d0b1d4da33406cf7b4
msgid "The ST-Link debugger should be connected to the STM32's JTAG connector using the JTAG breakout cable. Connect the SWDIO and SWCLK (see `Debug port pinout <https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/common-pixracer-overview.html#debug-port-jst-sm06b-connector>`__ for reference) to the corresponding SWDIO and SWCLK pins on the ST-Link debugger."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:61
#: 56575d85c08140ae9c1404e573537de7
msgid "Ensure :ref:`BRD_OPTIONS<BRD_OPTIONS>` sets the \"Enable Debug Pins\" bit if bit 3 is present in the vehicle software being used. It is also advised to disable the watchdog by ensuring bit 0 is not set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:66
#: 6e3d8a04f5ca4ab9886ff76da96ae936
msgid "Installing GDB"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:68
#: 1101ecfba24849dd8a66abd8e527e6c9
msgid "If using Ubuntu, GDB is likely already installed on your machine and it will likely work although we recommend using the version available for download here `https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Tools/STM32-tools <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Tools/STM32-tools>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:72
#: aa3b4f7a9964444d98866ff8b57cedc3
msgid "The gcc-arm-none-eabi*-linux.tar.bz2 file contains both the recommended compiler and the recommended version of gdb."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:75
#: 1046d0c36c5042888abbb2eebd5beaa1
msgid "If you will be using the ST-Link debugger, please install the gdb version found in the gcc-arm-none-eabi-6-2017-q2-update-linux.tar.bz2 file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:78
#: b87f25b2a7234401be445a851e7fcd8e
msgid "After installation you should find you have a tool called arm-none-eabi-gdb."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:82
#: 0b4dfcdebdea4eb0b5b5f76df826294f
msgid "Installing OpenOCD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:84
#: fa7b96721c6c49329b758867f40df63c
msgid "You will need to install OpenOCD if you are using the ST-Link debugger:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:86
#: 3432c0928c6d45ea90e9aa5a95902337
msgid "``sudo apt-get install openocd``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:88
#: 6a656e896ddc4a4f8eb1ce51f801939d
msgid "Before OpenOCD and GDB are run, their configuration files need to be copied to the build folder. Note that the build folder name is the same at the board name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:90
#: 95fe31199e7648babca97b8af736e9af
msgid "Go to the ``./Tools/debug`` folder and copy ``openocd.cfg`` to ``./build/<boardname>/bin``, if not done so previously"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:93
#: 21fa98ed04a842c6a40e333d7a48b79c
msgid "Type ``openocd`` in your terminal in the ``bin`` directory above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:98
#: 394b136806d54812aeae5881f14af120
msgid "Note: there are 2 versions of the ST-link debugger on eBay, so if the command does not work, change the first line to ``source [find interface/stlink-v2-1.cfg]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:103
#: 83ea2923fbb24442b65815c3d732b11c
msgid "Starting GDB and running some commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:105
#: 333fbc58479a4bb5b492421e45270bf6
msgid "Copy ``.gdbinit`` to ``./build/<boardname>/bin`` and edit ``~/.gdbinit`` to have the following text: ``set auto-load safe-path /``, if not done so previously."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:109
#: d3d30e84017d4b4baa8bdb732e54e54a
msgid "In another window, type ``arm-none-eabi-gdb arducopter`` in the ``./build/<boardname>/bin`` folder. Now you have connected to the gdb debugging session and can use the commands from the next section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:117
#: aae49a54c4c64372bc787908736e737a
msgid "Some useful commands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:119
#: b95a4e31d08c4145ac6585e7e209c74d
msgid "``r`` -- restarts the process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:121
#: a59239f5a4014c9fbb6155c63a76aef8
msgid "``b function-name`` -- i.e. b setup -- sets a breakpoint at the start of the \"setup\" function. Note a class name can be prepended such as ``b AC_AttitudeControl::init``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:126
#: e78ebed5bcee4a9e905f8bce74747170
msgid "If you are debugging a board using external flash and you receive \"Failed to read memory at 0x.....\", try \"set mem inaccessible-by-default off\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:128
#: e4758b71d40c4aecb390fd6fe1d02cfa
msgid "``Ctrl-C`` -- stops the code from executing so you can set breakpoints, etc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:131
#: 99721342a35b47aa9cf98c16acd26973
msgid "``continue`` -- continues the code from wherever it was stopped"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:133
#: bade8dad1c4346a8a0d83807e9448a3b
msgid "``show interrupted-thread`` -- shows address where execution has stopped (see below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:136
#: 900b9188e770477f90b23a3945b38b40
msgid "``info line * <address>`` -- shows c++ line for a given address (i.e. from show interrupted-thread)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:139
#: ff9cfa096bc44899833aeba7e7682de9
msgid "``info threads`` -- show status of all threads"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:141
#: 0160b16bb42c496e9ea8b550578173e0
msgid "``disassemble <address>`` -- converts given address into assembler code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/debugging-with-gdb-on-stm32.rst:143
#: cefbc32363774b86a599e034e6cd478d
msgid "``exit`` -- exits from the GDB"
msgstr ""
